[68.6162, "o", "Here's the audit summary:\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Edge Cases\r\n\r\n**`divide`** \u2014 returning `0.0` for `b == 0.0` is the critical flaw: it's indistinguishable from a legitimate `0.0 / x` result. Callers cannot detect the error. Should return `Option<f64>` or at minimum `f64::NAN`. Also: NaN inputs propagate silently (correct IEEE behavior, but undocumented).\r\n\r\n**`fibonacci`** \u2014 overflows silently at `n >= 94` in release builds (panics in debug). `fibonacci(94)` wraps and returns a wrong answer. Fix with `checked_add` and `Option<u64>`.\r\n\r\n**`word_count`** \u2014 no edge cases; `split_whitespace` handles multi-space, tabs, newlines, and leading/trailing whitespace correctly already.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Suggested Doc Comments\r\n\r\n```rust\r\n/// Divides `a` by `b`, returning `0.0` if `b` is exactly zero.\r\n/// NaN inputs propagate per IEEE 754. Zero divisor is silent failure \u2014\r\n/// result is indistinguishable from a legitimate zero.\r\npub fn divide(a: f64, b: f64) -> f64\r\n\r\n/// Returns the `n`th Fibonacci number (0-indexed).\r\n/// Pani"]
[68.6164, "o", "cs in debug builds for `n >= 94` (u64 overflow); wraps silently in release.\r\npub fn fibonacci(n: u32) -> u64\r\n\r\n/// Counts whitespace-delimited words. Empty or all-whitespace input returns 0.\r\npub fn word_count(s: &str) -> usize\r\n```\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Missing Tests\r\n\r\n| Function | Missing cases |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| `divide` | **zero tests exist** \u2014 need: normal, negatives, zero divisor, NaN, infinity |\r\n| `fibonacci` | `n=20`, `n=93` (last safe `u64`), `n=94` (overflow boundary) |\r\n| `word_count` | **zero tests exist** \u2014 need: empty `\"\"`, whitespace-only, tabs/newlines, multi-space gaps, single word |\r\n\r\nThe two highest-priority fixes: change `divide`'s return type to `Option<f64>`, and add `checked_add` overflow protection to `fibonacci`.\r\n"]
[68.6168, "o", "\u001b[?1006l\u001b[?1003l\u001b[?1002l\u001b[?1000l\u001b[>4m\u001b[<u\u001b[?1004l\u001b[?2031l\u001b[?2004l\u001b[?25h\u001b]9;4;0;\u0007\u001b]0;\u0007"]
